course: dictionary
lesson: 7536
title: Wobbles that take forever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Precession is a slow turning or wobble. Think of a spinning top: as it spins, its tip does not stay still but slowly draws a circle on the floor. That slow circle is precession.
explain: The Earth does the same thing. It spins like a top, and its axis, the imaginary line through the North and South Poles, wobbles very slowly in a circle. One full circle takes about 26,000 years.
explain: The clues in this sentence help: «The "Precession of the Equinoxes" is a real, very slow wobble of the Earth that takes about 26,000 years, so saying something happened "in the middle of" it one morning is Kipling's joke.» The words very slow and 26,000 years tell you that precession is far too slow to see in one morning.
fact: Precession means the slow turning of the axis of a spinning object, so that the axis traces a circle.
fact: A spinning top shows precession: its tip draws a circle as it wobbles.
fact: Earth's axis precesses slowly, taking about 26,000 years to make one full circle.
fact: Because of precession, the North Star changes over thousands of years.
exercise: What is precession? | The name for the Earth's oceans | The shape of a spinning top's handle | *A slow turning of the axis of a spinning object, so that the axis traces a circle | A fast spin that makes a loud noise
exercise: In science lessons, a spinning top wobbles in a circle. What is this called? | Reflection | Magnetism | *Precession | Gravity
exercise: Why does the North Star change over thousands of years? | The stars swap places every week | *Because Earth's axis precesses slowly | Because the North Star is a planet that moves | Because the Earth stops spinning each night
test: The Earth's axis takes about how long to complete one slow circle in precession? | *About 26,000 years | About a day | About one week | About a minute
test: In the sentence «The "Precession of the Equinoxes" is a real, very slow wobble of the Earth», what does the word very tell you? | That the wobble happens only once | That the wobble is fast | *That the wobble is extremely slow | That the Earth stops wobbling
exam: Which of these best describes precession? | The sound a spinning top makes on the floor | A map showing where the North Star is | *A slow wobble in which an axis traces a circle, like a spinning top | A quick flash of light from a star
